engthens-cfp-case-statement-win-smu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Vols lose top receiver Matthews to knee injury vs. Texas A&M","description":"Tennessee leading receiver Mike Matthews suffered a right knee injury in the second quarter of Saturday's game at Texas A&M.","published":"2026-11-14T23:16:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483677/vols-lose-top-receiver-matthews-knee-injury-vs-texas-am","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia commit, DL Marcellus Young Casario died after 'sudden medical emergency'","description":"Marcellus Young Casario, a Georgia football commit, died Friday after experiencing a \"sudden medical emergency,\" according to his high school.","published":"2026-11-14T20:36:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD rips Ole Miss, SEC; Rebels defend travel effort","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny ripped the SEC and Ole Miss for the \"inexplicable\" decision to move its game to Sunday, while the Rebels defended their travel efforts.","published":"2026-11-14T23:54:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Reynolds to have MRI on knee; backup Vizzina (ankle) also hurt","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds is having an MRI on his injured knee, and backup Christopher Vizzina was sent to the hospital to evaluate his ankle.","published":"2026-11-14T23:52:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State WR Smith sets Big Ten record, states Heisman case","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards while also making his Heisman Trophy case in Saturday's win over Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T23:15:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4921117/vicari-swain","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicari_Swain"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Vicari Swain","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vicari_Swain","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:07Z","intro":"Vicari S. Swain (born September 12, 2004) is an American college football cornerback and return specialist for the South Carolina Gamecocks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Swain grew up in Carrollton, Georgia, and started playing football at age six. He attended Central High School where he competed in football and baseball and was a top defensive back and wide receiver in the former. As a junior, he posted 55 receptions for 855 yards and eight touchdowns along with 28 tackles and six interceptions. Swain then recorded 44 receptions for 610 yards and seven touchdowns along with 35 tackles and six interceptions as a senior in 2022. A four-star recruit, he committed to play college football for the South Carolina Gamecocks."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Swain appeared in three games for the Gamecocks as a true freshman in 2023. He then made 13 appearances as a backup cornerback in 2024, recording 13 tackles and a sack. He became a top cornerback and return specialist for the Gamecocks in 2025. In the first two games, Swain had three punt return touchdowns, earning Southeastern Conference (SEC) Special Teams Player of the Week both times. He returned a total of 19 punts for 302 yards and three touchdowns during the season, tying Kaden Wetjen for most punt return touchdowns nationally. He also posted 28 tackles, five pass breakups and two interceptions on defense."}]}}